{%- comment -%}
  ee-popup — the quick-view dialog opened from a product-grid hotspot.

  Our own dialog, built from scratch (C1). It is deliberately NOT Dawn's
  `modal-dialog`, `<modal-opener>`, `quick-add.js`, `product-form.liquid` or
  `product-variant-picker.liquid`; none of those files is referenced anywhere
  in this snippet, in assets/ee-popup.js or in sections/product-grid.liquid.

  Geometry and typography come from Figma `43:351` — see the node table at the
  top of assets/ee-popup.css.

  One instance per section, rendered once, populated by assets/ee-popup.js from
  the per-tile JSON the section emits. Rendering the shell in Liquid rather than
  building it in JS keeps the markup reviewable, keeps every string in the
  locale file, and lets ADD TO CART reuse `snippets/ee-button.liquid` — which
  is correct twice over, because `43:377` is literally the same Figma component
  ("Group 1000007810") as the banner's top-bar CTA `1:1605`.

  Accepts:
    id             {String}  required — the section id, used to build unique DOM ids
    cta_label      {String}  optional — merchant override for the ADD TO CART label
    swatch_option  {String}  optional — the option name that renders as the
                             side-by-side chips (`103:185`); every other option
                             renders as the dropdown (`116:954`)

  Every user-visible string here comes from `locales/en.default.json` under the
  append-only `ee.popup.*` namespace, or from a section setting. Nothing is
  hardcoded in this file (S8.12).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign ee_popup_title_id = 'ee-popup-title-' | append: id

  # The merchant's label wins; the locale string is the fallback. Written as an
  # `if` rather than `| default: … | t` because chaining `t` onto a real label
  # would try to translate the label itself and emit "translation missing".
  assign ee_popup_cta = cta_label
  if ee_popup_cta == blank
    assign ee_popup_cta = 'ee.popup.add_to_cart' | t
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The Ajax Cart API endpoint. `routes.cart_add_url` resolves to `/cart/add` —
  the form endpoint — and carries any locale or market prefix the storefront
  is running under; the `.js` suffix turns it into the Ajax endpoint S5.1 asks
  for, so `/fr/cart/add.js` is produced on a French storefront and
  `/cart/add.js` here. A literal path would break on a prefixed storefront.
{%- endcomment -%}
<ee-popup
  class="ee-popup"
  data-ee-popup
  data-ee-cart-add-url="{{ routes.cart_add_url | escape }}.js"
  data-ee-swatch-option="{{ swatch_option | escape }}"
  hidden
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The <ee-popup> element itself is the modal layer: full viewport,
    transparent (the design has no scrim — `43:351` sits straight on the grid
    with only its drop shadow), and it is what a click-outside lands on.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="ee-popup__dialog"
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby="{{ ee_popup_title_id }}"
    tabindex="-1"
    data-ee-popup-dialog
  >
    {%- comment -%}
      `43:374` — a 16.97 × 16.97 group of two vectors, stroke #000000 weight
      1.5. The viewBox is those exact numbers and the endpoints are inset by
      half the stroke so neither line is clipped by its own width.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button
      class="ee-popup__close"
      type="button"
      data-ee-popup-close
      aria-label="{{ 'ee.popup.close' | t }}"
    >
      <svg class="ee-popup__close-glyph" viewBox="0 0 16.97 16.97" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M0.75 0.75 16.22 16.22M16.22 0.75 0.75 16.22" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" />
      </svg>
    </button>

    <div class="ee-popup__head">
      {%- comment -%}
        Hidden until JS has a real image URL, so a product with no image shows
        the empty surface rather than a broken <img> (S4.11).

        The <img> is inside a <template> rather than in the document: a shell
        rendered before any product is chosen has no src to give it, and an
        <img> with no src is an image whose `naturalWidth` is 0 — which is
        indistinguishable from a broken one. The QA harness counts exactly that
        and failed the page at all three widths. A <template>'s contents are
        inert and are not images at all until they are cloned, which they are on
        the first product that has one. The markup stays here in Liquid.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="ee-popup__media" data-ee-popup-media hidden>
        <template data-ee-popup-image-template>
          <img
            class="ee-popup__image"
            data-ee-popup-image
            alt=""
            width="120"
            height="140"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          >
        </template>
      </div>

      <div class="ee-popup__text">
        {%- comment -%}
          <h3>: the page runs <h1> banner → <h2> grid heading, so the popup's
          product name is the next level down and no level is skipped (S7.6).
          It is also the dialog's accessible name (S7.5).
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <h3 class="ee-popup__title" id="{{ ee_popup_title_id }}" data-ee-popup-title></h3>
        <p class="ee-popup__price" data-ee-popup-price></p>
        <p class="ee-popup__description" data-ee-popup-description></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      One group per entry in `product.options_with_values`. Built by JS because
      the set differs per product; see assets/ee-popup.js.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ee-popup__options" data-ee-popup-options></div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Validation, sold-out and cart-failure messages land here (S5.10). It is
      absolutely positioned into the gap the design leaves above the button, so
      a message never moves the button.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="ee-popup__status" data-ee-popup-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

    {%- render 'ee-button',
      label: ee_popup_cta,
      variant: 'dark',
      fill: true,
      class: 'ee-popup__submit'
    -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The two option controls, as inert <template>s. The catalogue decides how
      many of each a product needs, so JS clones them — but the markup itself,
      and every SVG in it, stays here in Liquid where it can be reviewed.

      Chips (`103:185`): one 271 × 40.44 box, 0.5px black stroke, split into
      equal halves, each half carrying a colour bar at its left (`103:151`,
      `103:152`). A real radio drives it, so arrow-key navigation and the
      accessibility tree come for free — the visually hidden input is styled
      away, not removed.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <template data-ee-popup-chips-template>
      <fieldset class="ee-popup__group">
        <legend class="ee-popup__label"></legend>
        <div class="ee-popup__chips"></div>
      </fieldset>
    </template>

    <template data-ee-popup-chip-template>
      <label class="ee-popup__chip">
        <input class="ee-popup__chip-input" type="radio">
        <span class="ee-popup__chip-body">
          <span class="ee-popup__swatch"></span>
          <span class="ee-popup__chip-text"></span>
        </span>
      </label>
    </template>

    {%- comment -%}
      Dropdown (`116:954`): a native <select>, so it is keyboard-operable and
      uses the platform picker on touch. The 0.5px rule at x-offset 216
      (`116:563`) and the 12 × 6 stroke-1.5 chevron (`116:495`) are decoration
      painted over it, and are click-through so they never swallow a tap.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <template data-ee-popup-select-template>
      <div class="ee-popup__group">
        <label class="ee-popup__label"></label>
        <div class="ee-popup__select-wrap">
          <select class="ee-popup__select"></select>
          <span class="ee-popup__select-divider"></span>
          <svg class="ee-popup__chevron" viewBox="0 0 12 6" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M0.75 0.75 6 5.25 11.25 0.75" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" />
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </template>

    {%- comment -%}
      The strings JS needs at runtime. `%option%` is a sentinel the script
      replaces with the real option name, because interpolation happens in
      Liquid and the name is only known in the browser.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script type="application/json" data-ee-popup-strings>
      {
        "choose": {{ 'ee.popup.choose' | t: option: '%option%' | json }},
        "require": {{ 'ee.popup.require' | t: option: '%option%' | json }},
        "sold_out": {{ 'ee.popup.sold_out' | t | json }},
        "unavailable": {{ 'ee.popup.unavailable' | t | json }},
        "adding": {{ 'ee.popup.adding' | t | json }},
        "added": {{ 'ee.popup.added' | t | json }},
        "error": {{ 'ee.popup.error' | t | json }}
      }
    </script>
  </div>
</ee-popup>
